<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1997/3/eng@/~part_III__cl_10__subsec_2> <https://schema.org/text> "Whenever it appears to any police officer of or above the rank of Inspector that there is reasonable cause to believe that in any premises there is concealed or deposited any evidence of the commission of an offence under this Act, and the police officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the object of the search is Hkely to be frustrated, he may exercise in and in respect of the premises all the powers mentioned in subsection (1) in as full and ample a measure as if he were empowered to do so by warrant issued under that subsection."@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1997/3/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1997/3/eng@/~part_III__cl_10__subsec_3> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#is_part_of> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1997/3/eng@/~part_III__cl_10> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1997/3/eng@> .
